<title>USA: Marathon raises U.S. posted crude 25 cts.</title>
<headline>Marathon raises U.S. posted crude 25 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it had raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.00 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.40 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $17.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.00.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
